      },
      "text": "FANCY BEAR (also known as Sofacy or APT 28) is a separate Russian-based threat actor, which has been active since mid 2000s, and has been responsible for targeted intrusion campaigns against the Aerospace, Defense, Energy, Government and Media sectors.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CrowdStrike_BearsintheMidst_DNC(06-04-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s9"
      },
      "text": "This adversary has a wide range of implants at their disposal, which have been developed over the course of many years and include Sofacy, X-Agent, X-Tunnel, WinIDS, Foozer and DownRange droppers, and even malware for Linux, OSX, IOS, Android and Windows Phones.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CrowdStrike_BearsintheMidst_DNC(06-04-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s15"
      },
      "text": "The COZY BEAR intrusion relied primarily on the SeaDaddy implant developed in Python and compiled with py2exe and another Powershell backdoor with persistence accomplished via Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) system, which allowed the adversary to launch malicious code automatically after a specified period of system uptime or on a specific schedule.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_17",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CrowdStrike_BearsintheMidst_DNC(06-04-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s17"
      },
      "text": "It consists of a single obfuscated command setup to run persistently, such as: powershell.exe -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -EncodedCommand",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_21",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CrowdStrike_BearsintheMidst_DNC(06-04-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "Powershell version of credential theft tool MimiKatz was also used by the actors to facilitate credential acquisition for lateral movement purposes.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_22",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CrowdStrike_BearsintheMidst_DNC(06-04-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s5"
      },
      "text": "FANCY BEAR adversary used different tradecraft, deploying X-Agent malware with capabilities to do remote command execution, file transmission and keylogging.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_23",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "CrowdStrike_BearsintheMidst_DNC(06-04-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s6"
      },
      "text": "It was executed via rundll32 commands such as: rundll32.exe “C:\\Windows\\twain_64.dll”",
